      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the quadratic polynomial \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we start by assuming the factored form of the polynomial is:\n\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q)\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are integers. Expanding the product, we get:\n\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nBy comparing coefficients with the original polynomial \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\), we identify:\n\n\\[\nb = p + q \\quad \\text{and} \\quad pq = 2008\n\\]\n\nWe need to find pairs of integers \\( (p, q) \\) such that their product is 2008. The steps are as follows:\n\n1. **List the factor pairs of 2008:**\n\n   The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\n   \\[\n   2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n   \\]\n\n   The factor pairs \\((p, q)\\) can be derived from these prime factors. We list all the positive factor pairs of 2008:\n\n   \\[\n   (1, 2008), (2, 1004), (4, 502), (8, 251)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\( b = p + q \\) for each pair:**\n\n   - For \\((p, q) = (1, 2008)\\):\n\n     \\[\n     b = 1 + 2008 = 2009\n     \\]\n\n   - For \\((p, q) = (2, 1004)\\):\n\n     \\[\n     b = 2 + 1004 = 1006\n     \\]\n\n   - For \\((p, q) = (4, 502)\\):\n\n     \\[\n     b = 4 + 502 = 506\n     \\]\n\n   - For \\((p, q) = (8, 251)\\):\n\n     \\[\n     b = 8 + 251 = 259\n     \\]\n\n3. **Identify the smallest positive value of \\( b \\):**\n\n   From the calculations above, the smallest positive value of \\( b \\) is:\n\n   \\[\n   b = 259\n   \\]\n\nThus, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
