      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) such that the quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) can be factored into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients. Two binomials of the form \\( (x + p) \\) and \\( (x + q) \\) can be multiplied to give:\n\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nGiven \\( pq = 2008 \\), we need to find pairs of integers \\( (p, q) \\) such that \\( p + q = -b \\). The goal is to minimize \\( b = -(|p| + |q|) \\).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of 2008. The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\n\\[\n2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n\\]\n\nThe factor pairs \\((p, q)\\) of 2008 are:\n\\[\n(1, 2008), (-1, -2008), (2, 1004), (-2, -1004), (4, 502), (-4, -502), (8, 251), (-8, -251)\n\\]\n\nWe will now calculate \\( |p| + |q| \\) for each pair and find the minimum value of \\( |p| + |q| \\).\n\n1. For \\((1, 2008)\\):\n\\[\n|1| + |2008| = 1 + 2008 = 2009\n\\]\n\n2. For \\((-1, -2008)\\):\n\\[\n|-1| + |-2008| = 1 + 2008 = 2009\n\\]\n\n3. For \\((2, 1004)\\):\n\\[\n|2| + |1004| = 2 + 1004 = 1006\n\\]\n\n4. For \\((-2, -1004)\\):\n\\[\n|-2| + |-1004| = 2 + 1004 = 1006\n\\]\n\n5. For \\((4, 502)\\):\n\\[\n|4| + |502| = 4 + 502 = 506\n\\]\n\n6. For \\((-4, -502)\\):\n\\[\n|-4| + |-502| = 4 + 502 = 506\n\\]\n\n7. For \\((8, 251)\\):\n\\[\n|8| + |251| = 8 + 251 = 259\n\\]\n\n8. For \\((-8, -251)\\):\n\\[\n|-8| + |-251| = 8 + 251 = 259\n\\]\n\nAmong these values, the smallest is 259. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) is:\n\n\\[\nb = -259\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
